title: CL4R1T4S study — prompt-technique findings + guardrails
summary: 'One-off team research into elder-plinius/CL4R1T4S (leaked production system prompts from ~25 AI products). Verdict: the "Fable boosts complete output" claim is a category error ("Fable" is a filename — ANTHROPIC/CLAUDE-FABLE-5.md — whose line-12 marketing copy was misread as a capability lever; the file is ~90% constraints and possibly partly synthetic). A prompt elicits latent capability, it cannot add it. BUT a real, bounded, adoptable upside exists: the agentic-persistence cluster from the coding-agent prompts. Adopt TECHNIQUE not TEXT — repo is AGPL-3.0, contains third-party proprietary text, and ships a live prompt-injection.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#agent-prompts'
  - '#orchestration'
learnings:
  - '''Fable boost'' = misread of marketing copy inside ANTHROPIC/CLAUDE-FABLE-5.md (line 12 ''sits above Claude Opus''); the file is constraints (refusals/child-safety/copyright), not a completeness amplifier, and references unverifiable products (likely partly synthetic). A prompt elicits, never adds, capability.'
  - 'Real adoptable upside = agentic-persistence cluster from coding-agent prompts: (1) explicit done-condition scoped to current intent ''do not yield until fully fulfilled'' (Factory DROID, Cursor), (2) mandatory self-verification before claiming done ''verify you edited ALL relevant locations'' (Devin <think>), (3) consult-source-before-acting / no-speculation (Factory; also Fable''s one real quality lever), (4) plan-before-act + todo checklist (Manus), (5) worked output-format exemplar (Codex). Incremental-compounding, not a step-change.'
  - 'Paradigm has a BETTER completeness target than the source prompts: bind the done-gate to the enumerable paradigm_ripple impact set + .purpose coverage (a checkable predicate) where DROID only has prose. Adoption targets: Completion Gate in OUTPUT_FORMAT_INSTRUCTIONS + no-speculation/pre-handoff-verify in BUILDER/REVIEWER/SECURITY prompts (packages/paradigm/src/core/agent-prompts.ts); no-premature-edit reinforcement in orchestration.'
  - 'GUARDRAILS: repo is AGPL-3.0 (viral) + contains other companies'' proprietary prompt text + ships a live prompt-injection in its README. Adopt the IDEA in our own words, NEVER paste text into any prompt/notebook/.purpose. Naive ''never stop'' fights the Stop-hook/soft-blocks — scope persistence to ''current claimed task'' so agents yield at a guard. Validate via A/B test before declaring a win.'
tags:
